lex-away.md`. The session goal itself is set by Alex's `/goal` command; the replacement text is given to him in the reply.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4879:## D440 · 2026-11-13 · Gate 2 failed; a memory diagnostic decides whether c15yc goes on (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4881:- **Council** (D439; Alex not active): an independent Codex member and Claude argued four rounds (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mj-*`). Agreed facts: gate 2 failed under its declared rules (two stop lines on the memory article); the link line measured the wrong thing (c8's request returns an uncovered statement with empty links); the 3-of-9 against 0-of-9 memory-thesis difference is real and its cause is not established. The council's first position was to keep c8; Claude's was a larger re-send. The consensus, after Claude adopted the council's changes (a margin fixed in advance, a three-way result in which inconclusive is not a pass, retained statements decisive, an exercised-control rule, a named and simulation-validated interval): \"Council position: consensus on the rule in mj-challenge-2.md as amended by mj-challenge-3.md\" (`mj-codex-4.md`).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4889:- **Next:** the council chooses the next step toward the PRD's production goal (D439).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4891:## D442 · 2026-11-13 · Next step: D431's same-day end-to-end comparison, run as a diagnostic (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4897:## D443 · 2026-11-13 · Shape B': an exploratory census of final-answer losses, the stored clean chain against fresh production v118 draws (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4902:## D444 · 2026-11-13 · Three fresh production draws under a corrected ledger, replacing the stopped ones (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4908:## D445 · 2026-11-13 · Next: a $0 source-to-answer trace of the clean path's 17 graded opening losses, memory first (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4