{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/DESIGN.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Citation-only judge version: closed id lists in the answer format (design, D712)\n     2\t\n     3\t**Alex's decision (D712, 2026-11-21):** \"开引用格式新版本 (推荐)\". The question offered: every id field of the judge's answer takes\n     4\ta closed list built from the request; a $0 check on stored data that accepted answers still pass and the bad ids are excluded; any\n     5\tpaid test asks him again.\n     6\t\n     7\t**Scope:** the answer format's four id fields only. Not changed:\n     8\t- the prompt text;\n     9\t- the request text;\n    10\t- the rung field;\n    11\t- `check_answer` and the retry;\n    12\t- the link direction (a separate design, D711).\n    13\t\n    14\t## 1. Census (stored data, $0)\n    15\t\n    16\t- **Refusals.** Every refused judge answer on the stored runs is an id-membership error: an id outside the list its field allows.\n    17\t  - 17 refusals in 5,408 distinct attempts: old-1, old-2 and old-3, plus the fresh calls of both pilot arms (Codex r37b; Claude's\n    18\t    script `id_typo_census.py`).\n    19\t  - All 5,389 committed answers fit the lists.\n    20\t  - The classes:\n    21\t    - a one-character copy of a listed evidence id: e3620 → e362, e3110 → e3111;\n    22\t    - a garbled evidence id (`e393`);\n    23\t    - a theme id in `cites_views` or in an evidence field;\n    24\t    - a dependency id used as an evidence id.\n    25\t- **List sizes per stored judge request** (`enum_size_census.py`; counting evidence twice, for cites and for push ids, plus themes and\n    26\t  dependencies), over 5,415 distinct requests (old-1, old-2, old-3; the pilots' fresh rows only, since their archives copy old-2's):\n    27\t  median 50–58 on the old runs and 160–183 on the pilots' fresh reader requests; p99 up to 573; max 909 (old-1 call 5652: 451\n    28\t  evidence ids, 7 themes, no dependency). 51 requests exceed 500. The two existing push enums add 6 values.\n    29\t- **Provider limits** (OpenAI structured outputs guide, read 2026-11-21):\n    30\t  - \"up to 1000 enum values across all enum properties\";\n    31\t  - above 250 values, \"the total string length of all enum values cannot exceed 15,000 characters\";\n    32\t  - all names, enum values and consts together at most 120,000 characters;\n    33\t  - `minItems`/`maxItems` supported;\n    34\t  - `$defs`/`$ref` supported;\n    35\t  - the guide does not say whether an empty enum is allowed, or whether a referenced enum counts once.\n    36\t\n    37\t## 2. Mechanism\n    38\t\n    39\tThe closing line of every request already forbids the wrong ids (`judging.py` lines 180–182: \"cites may name only the evidence ids\n    40\tlisted above; cites_views only the dependency thesis ids listed above; … a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or\n    41\tcites_views\"). The answer format accepts any string in those fields (`schema_for`, lines 55–75). So the prose rule is present and the\n    42\tmodel still breaks it: about 0.3% of answers overall, and 2.6% of linked readers' answers, whose requests carry a dependency block\n    43\tbeside the themes.\n    44\t\n    45\tThe code already decides membership after the answer (`check_answer`). Moving the same closed set into the format makes a wrong id\n    46\timpossible to write: code owns identity (AGENTS §2). The judge still decides what matters.\n    47\t\n    48\t## 3. The change\n    49\t\n    50\t- **Versions** (the D694 pattern: a new name for a changed judge, the old ones byte-identical):\n    51\t  - `judging-v9`: judging-v7's text and request, with closed lists.\n    52\t  - `judging-v10`: judging-v8's text and dependency block, with closed lists.\n    53\t  - The prompt files are copies, pinned to v7's sha. `SUPPORTED_VERSIONS` and the frozen tests extend; `schema_for('judging-v7')` and\n    54\t    `schema_for('judging-v8')` keep `JUDGING_SCHEMA_SHA`.\n    55\t  - Config: `poc-v121` = poc-v118 with `rejudging.prompt_version` = judging-v9 (the product with the fix). No config names v10 until\n    56\t    the link-direction design; v10 is built so the $0 test covers the dependency-block shape.\n    57\t  - Alternative (the council's call): a `rejudging.closed_lists` field instead of two names. Claude's lean is names: the archive,\n    58\t    harnesses and frozen tests already key on the version.\n    59\t- **The lists come from the request text that is sent,** read by the same parsers `check_answer` uses, so the format and the check\n    60\t  agree by construction:\n    61\t  - evidence ids: `evidence_shown_in(user)`;\n    62\t  - theme ids: `themes_shown_in(user)`;\n    63\t  - dependency ids: the resolved dependencies, exactly the set `check_answer` allows. A test asserts that this set equals the ids the\n    64\t    text lists.\n    65\t- **The fields:**\n    66\t\n    67\t  | Field | Closed list | With an empty list |\n    68\t  |---|---|---|\n    69\t  | `cites` items | evidence ids | `maxItems: 0` |\n    70\t  | `pushes[].evidence_id` | evidence ids | `pushes` gets `maxItems: 0` |\n    71\t  | `cites_views` items | dependency ids | `maxItems: 0` |\n    72\t  | `theme_pushes[].view_id` | theme ids | `theme_pushes` gets `maxItems: 0` |\n    73\t\n    74\t  Ids are listed sorted.\n    75\t- **Representation:** to settle before the build.\n    76\t  - (a) A plain enum per field: the stored max is 909 + 6 = 915 values, under 1,000.\n    77\t  - (b) One `$defs` evidence enum referenced by both evidence fields: 464 if it counts once, which is unverified.\n    78\t  - (c) A `pattern` alternation, as the pre-v74i extraction admission schema did (`folds_into`, removed with the frozen prompt). It\n    79\t    falls outside the enum count but under the 120,000-character total.\n    80\t  - Claude's lean: (a). It is the plainest, and every stored request fits.\n    81\t- **Over the limit:** a request whose lists exceed the provider's limits is refused before the send (`JudgementFormatError` → the\n    82\t  day's `judging_failed`, resumable). There is no silent fallback to open strings. No stored request reaches the limit.\n    83\t- **Building it:** `schema_for(prompt_version, evidence_ids=None, dependency_ids=None, theme_ids=None)`.\n    84\t  - In `round_of_judgements`, each view's schema is built beside its prompt (`prompts[v]` gains the schema), and `ask` sends it, the\n    85\t    retry included.\n    86\t  - For v7/v8 the lists are ignored and the schema is the frozen one.\n    87\t  - The schema name stays `judgement` (harnesses read it).\n    88\t\n    89\t## 4. Tables\n    90\t\n    91\t### 4.1 State × event\n    92\t\n    93\t| State / event | What happens | What is written; which date |\n    94\t|---|---|---|\n    95\t| First judgement (no previous conclusion) | the lists are built as for any request | the same as now |\n    96\t| No dependency (all of poc-v121) | `cites_views` has `maxItems: 0` | — |\n    97\t| No theme | `theme_pushes` has `maxItems: 0` | — |\n    98\t| No evidence shown (all hidden) | `cites`/`pushes` have `maxItems: 0`; such a view stays eligible only if evidence is in force | — |\n    99\t| A refusal on another check (rung, changed, stance) | the retry carries the same schema | as now: the refused row is retired |\n   100\t| Double refusal | the day fails, resumable; on resume the same text gives the same schema | as now |\n   101\t| Resume of a failed day | the same text and schema; already judged views are not re-judged | as now |\n   102\t| A theme closes or a dependency resolves between prompt and answer | the lists are frozen in the sent request; `check_answer` reads the same text | — |\n   103\t| Concurrent judge workers | one schema per view, built from that view's text | — |\n   104\t| The provider refuses the schema (HTTP 400) | a transport error → `judging_failed` → resumable | no answer row |\n   105\t| Lists over the limit | refused before the send, as above | no call |\n   106\t| The config changes between runs | the version is in each call's config record; the schema is in the archive key | a new key per request |\n   107\t| A valid id that names the wrong source | not detectable by code | measured separately (§6) |\n   108\t\n   109\t### 4.2 Value × reader\n   110\t\n   111\t| Value | Reader | Effect |\n   112\t|---|---|---|\n   113\t| The per-request schema | `model.build_request`, then `request_identity` (archive key) | every judge request under v9/v10 gets a new key: no stored answer is reused; a paired run needs its own replay proof (Codex r37b) |\n   114\t| The schema name `judgement` | `paid_run.is_judgement_request`, `july_test` | unchanged |\n   115\t| The schema | `preflight.py` (`SCHEMAS['judge']` = v7's) | unchanged for stored v7 rows; v9 rows are checked by `check_answer` as now |\n   116\t| The answer | `vocabulary.judgement_answer`, `_record` | the same shape |\n   117\t| The input size | cost | about 450 characters at the median, up to about 7,300 at the max, priced at $0.10 per million input tokens: negligible; measured in the $0 test |\n   118\t\n   119\t### 4.3 New path × old checks\n   120\t\n   121\t| Old check | Under v9/v10 |\n   122\t|---|---|\n   123\t| `check_answer`: evidence membership, deps, themes | still runs; never fires on a membership error the format holds; kept as the owner of the rule |\n   124\t| Rung range, first judgement must say changed, rung moved needs changed, stance fields non-empty | unchanged (out of scope) |\n   125\t| Frozen tests (prompt sha, schema sha) | v7/v8 unchanged; v9/v10 pinned: prompt sha = v7's; a schema test on a fixed list |\n   126\t| D359: refuse unbuilt versions | `SUPPORTED_VERSIONS` extended to the two names only |\n   127\t| Launchers: which config runs where | poc-v121 a product config (like poc-v118); v10 is named by no config |\n   128\t\n   129\t### 4.4 Prior decisions\n   130\t\n   131\t- D354 (the frozen judge; a change is a new version Alex opens) and D712 (opened).\n   132\t- D359 (the code builds only named versions).\n   133\t- D694 (v8 = v7's text, a new name for a request change).\n   134\t- D198 (the closed set is what the request showed).\n   135\t- D711 (the census and the recommendation).\n   136\t- The pre-v74i extraction admission schema constrained `folds_into` to the shown ids by pattern. It was removed with the frozen prompt\n   137\t  (commit 248ef1b4), not rejected by any decision found.\n   138\t\n   139\t## 5. The $0 test (registered before it runs)\n   140\t\n   141\t- **T1, the product path** (old-2 replayed under poc-v121).\n   142\t  - The harness transport answers each judge request with old-2's stored answer for the same system and user bytes.\n   143\t  - Every judge request's text must be byte-equal to old-2's; only the schema may differ.\n   144\t  - The transport validates the stored answer against the request's schema with a standard-library validator for the subset used\n   145\t    (object, array, string enum, integer, boolean, required, `additionalProperties: false`, `maxItems`).\n   146\t  - Pass:\n   147\t    - the replay completes and equals old-2's store, as the `neither` pass does;\n   148\t    - every accepted old-2 answer validates;\n   149\t    - each of old-2's 4 refused answers fails validation on the id that `check_answer` refused.\n   150\t- **T2, every stored shape** (offline).\n   151\t  - For every stored judge request of old-1, old-2, old-3, control-1 and linked-1, the lists are rebuilt from its text (v10 for\n   152\t    linked-1's dependency block) and the stored answer validated.\n   153\t  - Pass: all 5,389 committed answers validate; all 17 refused answers fail on their bad id.\n   154\t- **T3, empty lists.** A view with no dependency (or no theme) gets `maxItems: 0`. An answer naming one id fails; an answer with\n   155\t  `[]` passes.\n   156\t- **T4, the limits.**\n   157\t  - The max list size over all stored requests is printed with its enum count and characters, under the provider's limits.\n   158\t  - A synthetic request over the limit raises before any send.\n   159\t- **Mutants**, each caught by a test that passes on the unmutated code:\n   160\t  - the push field left open;\n   161\t  - lists built from the ledger instead of the text;\n   162\t  - `maxItems` dropped for an empty list;\n   163\t  - the validator's enum check removed.\n   164\t- **Prompt size:** the schema's characters and tokens before and after, median and max.\n   165\t- **The suite, the frozen tests and `docs/check.py`.**\n   166\t\n   167\t## 6. What the $0 test cannot show\n   168\t\n   169\t- Whether, with the lists closed, the judge picks the intended source. The e3111 case could become e3110 or e3112.\n   170\t- Whether the format changes the forecasts.\n   171\t\n   172\tA paid measurement shows both, and it is Alex's to open (D712). One way: re-send the stored refused requests and a matched set of\n   173\taccepted ones under v9, and read the cited sources beside the forecasts.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cat docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md; sed -n '260,495p' AGENTS.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Core PRD for the next phase: filing must recognise indirect relations the way an analyst does\n\n> Status: in progress (opened 2026-11-04). Alex: \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\".\n> This page is the single source for this phase. In a conflict: Alex's words → `docs/DECISIONS.md` → this page → the other design documents. This page's\n> conclusions, evidence, constraints, measuring method and process are not rewritten to follow test results;\n> test results go into `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md`, and changing this page first needs Alex's word.\n> Amended 2026-11-04 (Alex replied \"go\" to the proposed amendment; D360): §5.2 drops \"also file under the other party's question\" and puts two\n> sentences in its place, one on choosing and one on splitting; §6's decision rule is rewritten. How it came about:\n> `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/prd-amendment-proposal.md` and `log.md` rows 11–16.\n> 2026-11-05 (D368): translated into English on Alex's word (\"不，用英文吧\"); §4 corrected to name the frozen standard's version 5 and §5 given a status line, on his delegation (\"你要来帮我看到底做不做\").\n\n## 0. Checklist before every start (Alex: \"每次开始前都需要revisit\")\n\nBefore starting any step, finish these in order; if one cannot be done, do not start:\n\n1. Read §§1–8 of this page in full; read the last three rows of `log.md`, and confirm where the previous step stopped and why.\n2. Check against §3, \"not in scope\": what this step does is not in that table. If it is in the table, stop and take it to Alex.\n3. Check against §4, \"constraints\": this step changes nothing frozen; a change to the frozen extraction prompt is the one place §5 names, and Alex's\n   word for it is already given.\n4. If this step costs money: its predictions and stop conditions are written down and frozen as §7 says (with their sha256 recorded beside them); the\n   requests are rebuilt byte for byte as §6 says; the control is re-sent the same day.\n5. What goes to Alex: one conclusion, one recommendation, one test, after §7's rounds of review; no menu of options; in plain words (the opening of\n   AGENTS, \"Explain and answer as to a sixteen-year-old\").\n\n## 1. Goal (end to end)\n\nEach question's judgement must receive the facts that can change its answer; facts that no question receives, those that bear on no question, must\nnot be piled into some one question. What is measured is the final judgement (the frozen judgement ruler, reader B, at the window end 2026-07-14), not\nany one step's own score.\n\n## 2. The core blocker (proven)\n\n**The system uses a fact for a question only when the fact \"states exactly this question's own figure\". An analyst also reasons onward from a fact: the other party's figure in a deal, price and volume for a product's revenue, a product's variants for its launch, and so on. The filing step cannot do this; the judging step reasons onward once it has the facts.**\n\nThis one blocker has two faces (described earlier as \"two problems\"):\n\n- **The parking lot.** Filing does not recognise facts that bear on a question indirectly, so no question takes them; yet to be kept, a fact must\n  first be filed (D209, D264). So D273 added the fallback sentence, which parks them in NVIDIA's total-revenue question. Of the reports under the\n  total-revenue question, in the part the gold read, 32–39% are ones the standard does not keep, 31–44% are kept but used by none of the 22 questions,\n  and only 7–10% are what the gold actually uses to judge total revenue (three draws); 24–44% of the total-revenue question's judgement citations are\n  news about other companies or the whole market (Intel graphics-card retail prices, a gas-fired power plant in Taiwan).\n- **Narrow questions starve.** Questions that only indirect facts can answer do not receive them: the custom-chip question received none of Broadcom's\n  figures in any of the three draws, and judged \"below $40 billion\" in all three; the operating-margin and NVIDIA capital-spending questions received\n  nothing at all and were never judged.\n\n**Evidence:**\n\n| Evidence | Content | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| Filing recognises only \"its own figure\" | The model says \"Broadcom's AI chip revenue is not cloud providers' spending on custom chips\" and \"Google Cloud's backlog is not capital spending\"; on a neutral refiling (no question id named, the rule not shown), 23 of 42 facts that matter are still not filed | `probe-filing-account-d1.md`, `refile-no_fallback.json` |\n| The judgement reasons onward once it has the facts | The custom-chip question's request of 7-14, sent 3 times in each of the three draws: as it was, 9/9 \"below $40 billion\"; with the Broadcom, Trainium and other facts written in that draw's ledger added, 9/9 left the lowest rung (6 times $40–60 billion, 3 times $60–80 billion), reasoning as the two readers did (\"guidance $16 billion, about $64 billion annualised, less networking chips\") | `predictions-one-test.md`, `one-test-result.json`, `log.md` row 8 |\n| Where the parking lot came from | D273: with the fallback sentence added, the core items on the extraction ruler went 64 → 68; the extraction ruler does not look at which question a fact is filed under (AGENTS §7.1, \"What it does not measure\") | `docs/DECISIONS.md` D273 |\n| What the parking lot holds | The figures above; an independent reader on 12 random articles: of 25 misfilings as it was, 21 were parked in the revenue question; 8 and 5 with the fallback deleted | `sink_by_standard.py`, the independent reader's report (`log.md` row 8) |\n\nAll files above are in `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/` unless noted otherwise.\n\n## 3. Ruled out or secondary (outside this phase's scope, each recorded separately)\n\n| Matter | Conclusion | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| The argument card | Not built; its code is deleted (Alex: \"好，删掉卡片代码\") | `docs/research/2026-11-04-argument-record/log.md` rows 4–11 |\n| The arrows of the question graph | Really wired backwards: a seed question's arrow means \"supports\" (D208), while the judging code reads it as \"whose conclusion to read\" (PRD 06). As a result themes are judged only after the total-revenue question, so the total-revenue question reads the themes' conclusions of the previous day, and in draw 3 a chain of questions went wrong in turn. But it does not explain the misfiling (filing comes before judging), and the gold itself judges data-center revenue as \"total revenue × 92%\". A topic of its own; settled by D368 (item 4: the arrow means \"supports\"), its fix to be built and measured | `core-problem.md`, `review-core-codex.md` |\n| Code removes the total-revenue question's own figures | True (\"keep only the narrowest question\" takes a seed arrow for \"a narrower sub-question\"), but each draw it costs the total-revenue question only 0–2 of the facts it needs | `log.md` row 8 |\n| A filing re-check added at the end | Recovers some, and misfiles about as many (independent reader: about one misfiled for each one filed right); not the solution | The independent reader's report |\n| One general sentence, \"the other party's figure in a deal counts too\" | The custom-chip question gains, but it pulls Morgan Stanley's price for a Rubin rack from the Rubin revenue question to the capital-spending question, and leaves some facts with no home | `answers.json` (the two arms definition and definition_no_fallback), `measure-corrected.txt` |\n| Tightening D259's \"leeway\" | Alex's own decision; this phase does not overturn it | D259 |\n| Opening questions (the Ohio guarantee was not opened); the two readers' disagreement on the China-share question | Another class of problem, not in this phase | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/diagnosis.md` §0 |\n| Model drift | With the same requests, today about half as many facts go into the total-revenue question as on 11-03; the cause is not proven. Compare only with a control re-sent the same day, never with the archive | `log.md` row 6 |\n\n## 4. Constraints (what must not move, and why)\n\n- **The frozen ruler** (AGENTS §7.1, D261, D262): the extraction standard, version 5 (the signed version 3 with D248's seven boundaries and D250's four\n  evidence boundaries and counting unit), golden-v5, the seed questions and the judgement gold; not a word changes; a disagreement is a gap in the\n  system (D263).\n- **The frozen extraction prompt** (D274): v74i (`poc-v108`) does not change by a word; what this phase changes is the one place that holds the filing\n  rule (the description of the `links` field), made into a new version with a new configuration and compared with v74i. Alex has given his word for this\n  work (2026-11-04: \"好你去解决问题\", \"开始做\"); making it the default needs his word again.\n- **Frozen opening and judging** (D354): this phase does not touch them.\n- **The standard's text** (in translation): §6, \"file under the narrowest open question; when no question takes it, record no home and drop it, and read\n  each one at evaluation\"; §5.1, \"makes the answer to some question more or less likely\", with four paths, \"demand, supply, competition, pricing\"; §5.3,\n  \"another company's matter is not kept when one cannot say which question about the covered company it moves through a path such as demand, supply,\n  competition or pricing\".\n- **Decisions**: D207 (one home per fact, the narrowest question), D209 (no home means dropped, each one read), D259 (leeway: a figure question takes\n  \"the demand, supply, competition and pricing that make it more or less likely\"; the total-revenue question taking more is an accepted cost, \"bounded by\n  the narrowest-question rule and the driver questions\"), D265 (code keeps only the narrowest), D273 (the fallback sentence), D355 (the two failed tests\n  of the previous filing topic).\n- **Prompt principles** (AGENTS §6): carry only the standard and add no new rule; a general hedge-fund analyst: every rule and example reads the same\n  for a bank, a drug maker, a retailer or a chip company, names neither NVIDIA nor its products or figures, and is not taken from a test article; a\n  classification is written as a closed set with two or three examples per class, replacing the abstract wording; quality is not fixed by lengthening\n  the prompt: remove as much as is added, or write down the reason.\n- **Code decides only \"is it the same thing\", never \"does it matter\"** (AGENTS §2).\n\n## 5. What to do\n\nStatus: the links-rule version that carried items 1–3 (v74l) failed its one test (§8 step 5); D361 keeps the fallback sentence, so item 3 is not carried out. The plan below is kept as written.\n\n1. **Replace the abstract sentence \"makes the answer more or less likely through demand, supply, competition or pricing\" with the few classes in which an analyst recognises an indirect relation, written as a closed set, each class with two or three examples from other industries** (AGENTS §6: one\n   abstract sentence is a coin flip on every send; examples replace it). A first draft of the classes (checked against the standard line by line at\n   design time; it holds only meanings the standard already has):\n   - The question's own figure: this question's figures, guidance, estimates and revisions (estimates for another period or another population follow\n     the existing rule).\n   - The other side of the same money: a seller's revenue from the buyers the question counts; those buyers' orders and backlog with these sellers.\n   - Price and volume: a product's price or shipments, for the question on that product's revenue.\n   - Variants and parts: a product's variants, alternatives, key parts and schedule changes, for the question on that product's launch.\n   - Demand, supply and competition moves with a number: customers' orders and capital-spending plans, suppliers' capacity and prices, competitors'\n     sales and share, for the question they affect.\n2. **State how to file a fact when two specific questions both bear on it** (the problem the `definition_no_fallback` arm exposed: Morgan Stanley's rack\n   price was filed under the buyers' capital-spending question, and the seller's Rubin revenue question lost it). One home per fact (D207): file it under\n   the question its figure measures most directly (for example, a hotel's room rate goes under its room-revenue question, not under the\n   travellers'-spending question; a parts maker's revenue from carmakers goes under the carmakers' parts-spending question, not under a rival parts\n   maker's share question); when one sentence gives a separate figure for each of two questions, write two items, each filed under its own question\n   (code stores two items that quote the same sentence as one record linked to both questions); never also file it under a broader question about the\n   same company (the failure of D355's test 2: the model filed it under an NVIDIA revenue question as well). The original draft's \"when the other\n   party's question is open … file it there as well\" conflicted with D207 and was deleted on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement (D360).\n3. **Delete the fallback sentence** and return to the standard's §6: when no question takes a fact, it is not filed; code drops it as \"no home\" and\n   records it (D209), and evaluation reads each one.\n4. Change only the one place that holds the filing rule; report its length in characters before and after, and write down the reason for any growth\n   (this time's reason: examples replace one abstract sentence).\n\n## 6. How to measure (the ruler does not move; the method does not change again)\n\n- **Requests**: rebuild each stored request byte for byte with the production code, changing only the one place that holds the filing rule; the\n  rebuilt request's archive id must equal the original's, or it is not sent (`resend_filing.py`, AGENTS §5). Never re-send the archive's copy whose\n  keys were sorted alphabetically.\n- **Articles**: development set = the 54 articles of `selection.json` (already read many times); held-out set = articles the extraction gold read and\n  the judgement gold uses that are not among those 54, drawn once before the test, with the list frozen and never changed afterwards. Both sets are\n  measured and reported apart.\n- **Control**: the unchanged requests re-sent 3 times the same day. No comparison with the archive (model drift).\n- **Each answer**: goes through the production code checks and filing first (including \"keep only the narrowest\" and \"no home means dropped\"), and is\n  counted after.\n- **What is counted** (`measure_filing.py`, with its matching rule fixed: items are matched on the distinct numbers and the proper nouns other than\n  NVIDIA in the source text; a source passage the system quotes that overlaps the gold's passage also counts as the same matter; \"optional\" counts as\n  optional; the citations in the body of the gold's answers are read):\n  - whether each fact that matters (one the gold uses to judge any question) reached the question that uses it, counted per fact, not per \"fact ×\n    question\";\n  - per question: the facts that matter that reached it and the new noise that appeared, counted by the decision rule below;\n  - the parking lot: how many facts the total-revenue question (v1, together with v22) takes in, and what they are;\n  - noise: how many of the sentences the standard does not keep are kept; per question, how noise is filed (links on facts the standard does not keep\n    or no question uses);\n  - how many core and supporting facts appear; the facts that matter that are dropped; how many questions each fact is filed under on average.\n  - Matching still has a small error (spot check: the new rule mismatches a few and misses a few); say so when reporting the numbers, and read the\n    ones that matter one by one.\n- **Decision rule** (rewritten on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement, D360. The original draft required \"every draw above the highest of the control's\n  three\" and the like, which the control itself fails when measured again, so it cannot tell good from bad. Script `decide.py`; written down and frozen\n  before each test; each draw's numbers and the totals are all reported):\n  - **Totals, with luck ruled out first**: each article's 6 answers from the new and the old arm are randomly reassigned between the two arms 4,000\n    times (with a fixed random seed); the new rule's difference counts as a real change only when fewer than 5% of the reassignments reach it.\n    - Development set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must rise; the count under the total-revenue questions (v1, v22) must\n      fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core facts must not fall.\n    - Held-out set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must not fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core\n      facts must not fall.\n  - **Per question, counted by code against the gold** (development and held-out sets together):\n    - A fact that matters which reaches the question at least two fewer times under the new rule than under the control counts as \"one fewer\" for that\n      question; in under the control all three times and under the new rule none of the three, it counts as \"lost outright\". A move to another question\n      that the gold also uses it for and that is no broader than the original (one home per fact, D207) does not count as fewer; a move to a broader\n      question counts. \"One more\" in the opposite direction offsets it.\n    - A noise sentence (not kept by the standard, or kept but used by no question) that the new rule files under the question at least twice while the\n      control never does counts as \"new noise\"; filed all three times, it counts as \"outright new noise\". The opposite direction offsets it.\n    - Any question with a net 3 fewer, a net 2 lost outright, a net 5 more new noise, or a net 3 more outright new noise fails. These thresholds are the\n      smallest values that keep \"misjudged when new and old are exactly the same\" within about one in ten; at the test, first compute the\n      misjudgement rate from the reassignments; if it is above one in ten, raise the threshold most prone to misjudgement by one step, then compare with\n      what was measured.\n  - **Smaller changes** (a question 2 fewer, two or three more noise) cannot be told from luck in three measurements: all are listed, given to a reader\n    who did not write the rule to read against the raw answers, and written into the report; they do not decide pass or fail.\n  Only when everything passes does it become a candidate; a candidate runs end to end three times on the 14-day window (extraction re-sent, matching and\n  judging run as usual, scored on the frozen judgement ruler), and that step needs Alex's word.\n\n## 7. Process (no drift)\n\n- **One recommendation and one test at a time** (AGENTS §7.3, Alex: \"就测试一种，一次\"): write the design first and put it through rounds of review (own\n  checks, Codex read-only, a reader who did not write it reading the raw records) until a round finds nothing serious; write down and freeze the\n  predictions and stop conditions; test once; if it does not match, stop and take it to Alex (D355: \"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\").\n- **A review's report is a lead**: each finding counts only once it is checked against the records (AGENTS §1).\n- **A prompt audit before any prompt change** (`.claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md`): check the whole request against the standard sentence by\n  sentence, in both directions.\n- **Every step goes into `log.md`**: what was done, what came of it, the files; mistakes and overturned results stay in it too.\n- **Do not repeat what was ruled out** (§3).\n\n## 8. Steps and where we are\n\n| # | Step | Output | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Design: the classes of indirect relation (a closed set + examples from other industries), how to file when a fact measures both sides, deleting the fallback; checked against the standard sentence by sentence; length before and after | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/design-links.md` | Done (draft 3, v74l / poc-v115) |\n| 2 | Checks at no cost: a sample answer written by the new rule goes through every code check; the new rule's text goes through the prompt audit | Same as above | Done |\n| 3 | Review rounds (Codex, independent readers, own), until nothing serious remains | `review-links-*.md` | Done (Codex 7 rounds, independent readers 3 times; round 7 found nothing serious) |\n| 4 | Draw and freeze the held-out set; write down and freeze this test's predictions and decision rule | `heldout.json`, `predictions-links.md` | Done (sha256 recorded for both) |\n| 5 | Test once: development set + held-out set, the new rule and the same-day control 3 times each | `answers-links.json`, `log.md` | Done (2026-11-04): failed: facts that matter reaching the right question, development set +7 (p 0.26); every other condition passed |\n| 6 | If passed: to Alex, to decide whether to run three 14-day end-to-end draws; if failed: stop, to Alex | `design-links.md` §8 | Stopped, to Alex |\n| 7 | (D361, Alex: \"按照你的提以来，但是你一定是自己反思多轮之后才给出的行动\") Measure the ceiling first: hand the source passages the gold cites straight to the frozen judgement; the custom-chip, operating-margin and capital-spending questions judged 3 times each at the window end, the custom-chip question as it was 3 times as the control; the fallback sentence is not deleted for now | `reflection-v74l.md`, `oracle-design.md` | Done: operating margin grounded 3/3, capital spending 2/3, custom chips 0/3 (the gap is in interpretation); the next step waits for Alex |\n| 8 | (D362, Alex: \"你继续啊不要scope drift and strongly follow evidence of your discovery and learning\") Two small changes where facts are not delivered, one at a time: ① when a quote is rewritten, code matches it back to the source sentence (changing nothing the model sees; verified by replaying the archive); ② a figure question's description states which figures it is derived from by definition (first sent 3 times each on the article that motivated it) | `delivery-fixes.md` | Stopped: an independent check overturned the first change's code (it would take in wrong figures); the second failed its trial send (1/3). The root: the signed standard's §5.3 does not keep two key facts, treating them as \"a restatement of known facts\" (proposal 6, awaiting approval); to Alex |\n| 9 | **Historical; superseded by D370.** (D363, Alex: \"乙\") At coverage start, record each question's starting figure once from the company's latest earnings report; the daily path still takes no restatements: design, rounds of self-checks and independent checks, validated first on the archive in the simplest way | `baseline-design.md` | Validated on two questions: the frozen extraction does not read the report's tables (0/3); with each question reading the report once on its own, the operating-margin question read its starting figure 2/3 and the capital-spending question 3/3, and the judgement then judged right (2/3, 3/3), about 2.5 cents. All 22 questions tested once (2026-11-05, Alex: \"你充分验证\"; files chosen by code, a same-day control, about $0.43): v10 and v12 judged right 9/9 each; no question already judged right turned wrong; but 5 of the 53 figures read were other quantities (the Vera CPU question and the Blackwell and Rubin question took a larger or neighbouring revenue line), so it failed condition 3, written beforehand. The model itself pointed to the reading instructions' sentence \"write the lines it is computed from, or the line the report uses for it\"; stopped, to Alex. Alex: \"改\"; only this sentence was changed (\"write only the lines it is computed from, or the same quantity under another name; never a broader line or a line next to it\"), tried on 4 questions first, then tested on all 22 (about $0.36): all three conditions passed: v10 and v12 9/9 each, no question judged right turned wrong, and all 46 figures were the questions' own quantities. Checked after an independent reader's challenge: the new sentence made the reading miss the capital-spending line in 3 of 12 reads, and it had been tested only on the one May report; the fourth version (a line-by-line re-check after writing) removed too much and failed; after a census of every failure trace (Alex: \"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信\"), the third version with the repaired quote check was chosen (D365): 0 wrong figures on the held-out August report; built into the production system (poc-v116; the $0 checks and the tests all pass). The full acceptance, three 14-day draws (Alex: \"跑验收\"; a same-day control; about $4.79): all passed: operating margin and capital spending judged right 3/3 each (the control never judged them), 53 against 45 in total (of 57); for the China-share question, the only one two fewer, both readers found the starting figures did not lead it astray. Alex: \"都做\": poc-v116 became the default (D366); the code was committed and a PR opened |\n\n## 9. Alex's own words on this matter (in time order)\n\n- \"你这个单独开一个专题出来解决 … 是promot，是系统结构设计还是到底哪里有问题挂错一堆东西，机制是不是有问题（一定要挂吗？有没有可能是杂音\" (2026-11-03)\n- \"So if it's a customer problem or other companies that you think is relating NVIDIA and it's the wrong evidence, then what is the standard for it? … from a hedge fund analyst standpoint, are these even relevant? Do you think your ruler is wrong in this aspect?\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"你确定下你接下来要改进的量化目标，以及你要看到端到端我们的管线是要做什么的，不要乱硬优化，要看到目标\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"就测试一种，一次 … 能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"这些只是类型题，你需要抽象拔高我们现在的核心问题和卡点。这个很重要这样改下去才是对的\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"go\" (2026-11-04, on the proposed amendments to §5.2 and §6 and on this test)\n  system and the gold is a gap in the system to close (D263), never a case for the ruler. A suspected inconsistency between gold and\n  standard no longer stops an arm: record the concern separately, continue scoring on the unchanged frozen gold, and disclose it with the results (D373).\n  What it measures: extraction against the gold's items, questions against must_open / may_open, the judgement at the window end\n  2026-07-14 against reader B's ranges (a numeric question agrees when the gold range overlaps the chosen rung's band, a yes/no question\n  when the answers match). What it does not measure: the judgement's daily path, and whether evidence was filed under the right question.\n- **The extraction standard** (piece 1) is the extraction step's PRD, signed by Alex on 2026-10-29 (D243: \"其他几条的意见我都ok，sign off\"),\n  which replaced the first version (D229: \"按照这套标准来开始做测量，这条标准不要漂移\"). It holds the ledger's three records, the five question\n  types, the opening tests, the evidence rule and its reject list, source tiers, weight, and how a prompt change is written, measured and\n  iterated. No arm, gold, judge or prompt adds a rule, an example or a weight the page does not hold; a change is a recorded decision in\n  Alex's words first, then a new version of the page, then a drift review.\n- **A ruler or gold that is built and reviewed is never changed again** (D261). Reviewed means readers who did not write it have read it\n  against the decisions and Alex has signed it. A ruler under construction is edited only until that review, and nothing is scored\n  against it before.\n- **The ruler is Alex's, never your own.** Gold, unit and the judge's reading are checked against what the product uses and fixed with\n  Alex before the first arm. A standard or reference you write gives every sentence its source (the signed standard, a decision, a PRD)\n  or lists it for Alex's decision with a lean; settling wording is no licence to change behaviour. After each rewrite, a read-only Codex\n  review against the decisions looks for unsourced rules, contradictions and misquotes, round after round until only wording-level\n  findings remain; clarity is tested apart, by independent readers on cases fixed before the text changes. A failed registered acceptance\n  stops the line and goes to Alex with its census; the next arm is never designed alone.\n- **Nobody grades their own change with a ruler still being corrected.** The reference is one Alex can read, reviewed and frozen before\n  the arms; a number scored against a ruler its author keeps correcting is not a conclusion. Meaning is judged by a reader who did not\n  write the change; code checks only structure and counts (Alex, 2026-10-29: \"我根本无法相信你的评价\").\n- **A new gold** (only for a new ruler version Alex opens). The unit is fixed before the first send (for extraction, one research matter\n  in one article, which several records may express; signed standard §11) and the gold is written from the complete material the model\n  sees before any answer is read. Each item holds the exact source span (checked by code), the standard line it follows, its weight under the signed rule and, where\n  proposals are pending, its weight under them with the proposals it depends on named.\n  A blind second reader reads the same sources; every disagreement is decided against the source and its reason recorded. The gold is\n  frozen with its sha256 and never edited after a send. Model-authored gold and model judges are labelled as such. A held-out set no arm\n  has seen is in from the first arm.\n- **Measure the stick before using it:** control against a second control, the criterion's null estimated (a conjunction over many items\n  fails by chance), and its workload sized from its rules. Tune on dev; score test once per configuration.\n\n### 7.2 Reading results\n\n- **A score is a lead; the traces are the measurement.** Every measurement has a score, and every time you read the traces yourself: the\n  raw answer beside the article for every missed helpful entry, and a sample of the extras and of the hits; historical gold keeps its original labels. The scorer\n  hard-codes no rule of the standard: it reads the gold file it is given, prints the gold's and the standard's sha256, and refuses a gold\n  made for another version; scores are compared only on the same gold. Do not write a new scorer to judge a probe: read the traces yourself (Alex, 2026-11-08:\n  \"不要写评分器这个之前就出问题过，你自己读trace 来分析\"). Alex, 2026-10-29 (D244): \"我觉得这是最容易出错的问题；你非常容易写死，我们在改的过程中如果drift你会一直用久的标准来衡量，这边需要有打分，但是“一定”要你自己下去看trace这是必须，记起来\".\n- **The ruler counts only what it was built to count.** Before a quality claim, a reader who did not write the change also reads the\n  fields the product stores (original day, original speaker, tier, the summary's hedges) and what the next step does with the record\n  (Alex, 2026-10-30: \"现在到底质量怎么样你深度的解析不要只是看尺子\").\n- Read the judges' reasons, not only the scores, and pick the next fix from the largest cause. Open the samples behind a metric's largest\n  values before reading it, and write down what a derived number reduces to.\n- **Report every number, regressions first.** For future evidence evaluation, combine the existing gold's core and supporting entries as helpful, use its not-kept entries as unhelpful, and leave optional entries neutral (D372). Count one research matter in one article (D250), not raw sentences. Retain the old labels and scores in historical results, and do not silently relabel the frozen gold. One quantity per table column. A comparison of\n  totals uses three draws; a count from one draw is labelled one draw and shows a mechanism, not a difference between arms. Lead with the\n  mechanism and the share of its class it explains, then the fix.\n- **Read what was dropped.** A statement the pipeline drops is thrown away with its reason, never parked on a side list; evaluation\n  reads the dropped statements by hand, classifies them by the mechanism that would have kept them, and fixes the largest class upstream\n  (D209: \"if it doesn't matter, just fucking throw it away … if there are false positives that got thrown away … you got to pick it up\").\n- **Measure end to end before a step's arm, and read the parked designs first.** A step's noise that the next step removes is not the\n  defect, and a step's recall that the next step throws away is. Before any arm on one step: the production replay through the whole path\n  on the gold window, the count at the step the product reads, and the decisions on the topic read for a parked fix (Alex, 2026-10-31:\n  \"make sure we are not going around in circles using wrong ruler and wrong prompts that don't work\"). Before a phase targets one step,\n  the upside of that step done perfectly is measured where the product is judged: the judge is given the gold's own evidence, built by\n  the production code, a few sends (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"我很不开心你的失败，为什么，深度多轮检讨记录，想思路突破\").\n- **Read what was kept against the gold, blind, before the next noise arm.** The not-kept gold entries a version keeps are judged by a\n  reader who wrote neither the gold nor the prompt, mixed with controls it cannot tell apart; where it parts from the gold, the standard\n  is unclear or the gold misreads it, and that goes to Alex before any arm counts it as noise (Alex, 2026-10-31: \"你再次重新检查尺子，看看是不是这些留下的还有歧义；然后再思考怎么降低noise\").\n- Pair every structural check with its semantic one. Run a data rule over its whole input range and on cases it was not tuned on. Weigh\n  a case by what it carries in the product, not by count.\n- A claim about a population (\"the data is clean\") rests on a code sweep of the whole population and an independent read of a fresh\n  random sample, never on the pages the author looked at.\n- Cost is priced from tokens at the published rates (`hivemind.model.PRICES`, cached input at `model.CACHED_INPUT_SHARE`), never from a\n  stored `cost_usd`; say which rates a projection uses.\n\n### 7.3 Iterating\n\n- **One class at a time** (Alex, 2026-10-29: \"你一类一类改，快速迭代然后测regression\"). Count the misses by mechanism; take the largest\n  class; trace it to the sentence that causes it; change one thing aimed at that class; run the whole bench (a prompt change alters every\n  request) against the previous version; read every regression to its raw answer. The pages that showed the failure locate its\n  mechanism; only the whole bench (every set, every draw) accepts the change.\n- **Name the effect on the judgement first.** Every proposed change states the effect it is expected to have on a reader or on the final\n  judgement, and is tested there where possible; a step's own counts do not decide it alone. A fix that keeps moving its error to\n  neighbouring cases stops being tuned on that set (Alex, 2026-11-09: \"感觉现在一直在修一些mknor的原地打转，你是不是要思考下现在具体还差什么high priority big impact 的需要做？\";\n  he approved this rule the same day, D391).\n- **A model call is a sampler.** Re-send a stored request before calling its answer a defect. Totals and acceptance come from at least\n  three samples beside a fresh control; a bar the control fails against itself judges nothing. A direct-read pass\n  (one send per article, every answer read beside its source; D238) locates mechanisms; its counts are one draw and are labelled so.\n- **A written log.** One row per arm: hypothesis, change, numbers against the control (regressions first), kept or not. Refuted arms and\n  your own mistakes stay in it; the next session starts from its last row.\n- **Own the loop, within what Alex agreed.** When the direction is agreed and no stop is in force (`CURRENT_STATE.md`), push your own\n  hypotheses through $0 checks and probes of a few cents on stored cases without asking. A registered test, an end-to-end run, or\n  anything that departs from the agreed plan starts on his word; a result that contradicts the hypothesis stops the line and goes to him\n  (D355: \"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\"). While he is not active (D439), \"his word\" is the council's\n  recorded consensus, and a stopped line goes to the council for re-assessment.\n- **Council before every change is sent.** A prompt, schema, code or criterion change, including one found by reading a probe, is a new\n  arm. It goes to an independent Codex read and a challenge round before its first send, and its result goes to a challenge round\n  before the next change. Reading the traces and the model's own account locates a fix; it does not review it (Alex, 2026-11-08:\n  \"你这些改动有我你有好好的跑council 再下手\").\n  Every round's reasoning and decisions are reflected on in the council until there is a consensus; the decision is recorded, and\n  the next test goes straight ahead, held to the PRD and its quantified goals, with every trace read by you yourself and not only\n  by readers (Alex, 2026-11-10: \"你应该跑council loop 来reflect 你每一轮的思路还有决策，需要你打成共识，记录决策，向前直行测试。不要drift,我们有PRD和量化目标，\n  你自己作为llm 下去看所有trace\").\n- **Small first, then one run.** A hypothesis is first validated the simplest way, on a few stored cases and a few cents, and shown to\n  work at a high level before any full analysis or stability test is built (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"don't overspend resources on wasting time.\n  We need to validate the hypothesis in a very simple way and to make sure that it works on a high level before we dive into do the full\n  analysis stability test. This is a principle you should remember\"). A day or week slice before any whole-corpus run; preflight on\n  stored data before any paid run (§5); no edit while a run is live (§9). A paid run measures a configuration; it never tries a fix.\n  Before each send, write what it can still change in the decision and which risk the cheaper check left uncovered; a replicate or\n  control that only re-measures noise or a settled comparison is not sent, and a fix is not sent before the model's own account and the\n  request locate where the decision is made (Alex, 2026-10-30: \"你跑这么多次真的有意义吗\"; \"我感觉你在为了跑而跑\"). Several fixes on one\n  base are each proved on stored data in minutes and then run together once (Alex, 2026-11-02: \"快速验证。不要drift,不要跑超级繁琐的全方位验证，先poc 改，能work,有结论，全部改动放到一起再跑完整\"; D266).\n- **One recommendation, one test.** What reaches Alex as the next step of work is one recommendation and one test of it, reached after\n  rounds of review (Claude's own, Codex's, an independent reader's) on the traces until a round finds nothing serious; never a menu of\n  arms or options, never a conclusion the next probe overturns (a choice that changes what the system does still goes to him with its\n  options and a recommendation, Authority and scope) (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"就测试一种，一次 … 你就没有自己看5轮review，能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议？\").\n  An agreed recommendation is first challenged by an independent reader on the concrete evidence behind it (\"why you give\n  recommendations for this. What did you see exactly?\"). A review round reads a rule as its author meant it; only a send shows how the\n  model applies it: before a registered test, the changed request is sent on the cases that motivated it, a few cents.\n- **A failed arm is diagnosed before the next one.** When an arm fixes its class and regresses another, write the root cause first: the\n  process error (what grew, what the small sample did not guard) and the mechanism, traced to the raw answers and the model's account,\n  never a guess stated as the cause. A small sample guards every class the change can move, not only its own. When a fix keeps moving\n  another class, the call is doing several jobs: move the rule to its owner (a field's definition sits in the schema beside the field)\n  rather than add a sentence (Alex, 2026-10-30: \"那你这些修改都是失败的呀，为什么，根因，你要检讨然后再接着尝试。我觉得你已经陷入deep loop 了\").\n  A failed step of a plan is fixed and re-run at that same step: its failures are the work list, and nothing later in the plan and no\n  substitute plan starts before it passes (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"你为什么要drift? 你现在明明还有这么多的问题要fix,你到底知不知道你要fix什么？\").\n  Before a fix is proposed, write which goal the mechanism still serves and what the product already gives for it; a measurement that\n  removes the reason a mechanism exists retires the mechanism instead of starting its repair (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"I told you to think about\n  it and you're giving me suggestions that you reject yourself\").\n- **Before a version is rejected, the rejection is checked.** Every failed or refused answer behind a \"did not pass\" is read against its\n  source and put down as the model's error or the measuring rule's or check's error; a rule or check that refuses right answers is fixed,\n  and a version that already meets the goal (what it was built to fix is fixed, nothing that was right turned wrong) is not dropped for a\n  stricter rule a later review added. Alex, 2026-11-05: \"你到底是不是再搬石头砸自己的脚？各种reject自己，你确定是正确的rejection 吗？你又下去看trace吗？\";\n  \"你不能每次都这样判错然后浪费我时间，我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信下一步你要跑什么才能收敛\".\n- **Correct, then cheap.** Make the pipeline right and stable before any cost, speed or throughput work; report cost as a baseline only\n  (Alex, 2026-10-25).\n\n## 8. Product thinking\n\n- Think like a hedge-fund analyst. A thesis is an argued view about the business and the world; its stance comes from the argument\n  weighed against what is priced. Extract the few metrics or segments that carry it; financial-statement lines are its evidence, never its\n  definition.\n- **Lean cautious, catch the increment.** Most of what an item says is noise: not everything is evidence and not everything is a lead. A\n  typical claim or background line is common knowledge (what an analyst following the company knew before the item) and is not kept\n  without a number and a specific narrative; new information that changes an answer is never missed. Alex, 2026-10-29 (D243):\n  \"不是什么事情都是惊弓之鸟需要抽取，杂音还是很大的，我们整体应该倾向谨慎不要看什么都是线索的感觉，但是同时我们要敏感一些新的信息带来的增量不要错过\".\n- **A senior analyst's granularity.** A question is a bet an analyst would hold a card for: a big matter, never trivia (a deal, product or\n  project opens one only when its scale can change revenue, profit, cash or credit risk). Small matters open no question, and whether\n  their statements are kept follows the evidence rule; wordings, deadlines, milestones and periods of one bet are one question, and a\n  statement carried by several outlets is one statement (how code applies it: §3, Identity). Two questions stay apart only when their answers can move apart and an analyst\n  would bet on each separately (D248). Alex, 2026-10-30: \"我觉得核心就是这个颗粒度的把控要符合一个高端的hedge fund analyst 的思维。不要搜集一堆鸡毛蒜皮的事情，要看重要的大事，合并整合关键的信息，这个是这个步骤的原则\".\n- The extraction standard (§7.1, piece 1) is the step's standard. Its two sources are applied before designing a prompt, evaluation or\n  change (D228): the thesis library's four evidence tiers (`docs/prd/06-views.md`, Four evidence tiers) and the investment-question\n  reasoning in the 90-thesis review (`research_notes/对冲基金论点粒度与金标/codex-challenger.md`, section 1; research, not a replacement for\n  recorded decisions). Source type and what a claim can support are separate judgments; no tier has a fixed score. Ask what revenue,\n  profitability, cash risk or competitive position the information can change; then separately decide whether it supports an existing\n  question or merits a new one. Indirect, incomplete and forecast information is evidence under the routing rules; none of those\n  properties, nor an inability to open a new question, alone makes it worthless.\n- Evaluate the overall research judgment against the source, the existing question and the evidence. Gold examples teach the reasoning\n  and its boundaries; reasonable alternative wording, evidence strength and inference are allowed (D226, D228). Record material factual\n  errors, unsupported assumptions and downstream losses separately. Do not turn a review's questions, output labels or optional details\n  into an automatic all-or-nothing score. Missing market expectations or historical context means that aspect was not tested, not that\n  it passed or failed.\n- When a thesis-quality check fails, look first at the unit of thought (are these the arguments that move the stock?), not deeper into\n  the numbers. Numbers are verified by code where they exist.\n- Outcomes are tracked and shown, never a gate on what a view may say. Missing data is \"no data to verify\", never a pass or a fail. A\n  repeat is not new evidence, and model agreement is not corroboration.\n\n## 9. Workspace and operations\n\n- Inspect a path before writing to it; new stored data gets a new, dated name; chain guarded steps with `&&`. Deleting stored data needs\n  Alex's request, a backup, exactly identified items and a log entry.\n- Absolute paths. Commands run under zsh: pass a list as an array. No foreground `sleep`.\n- Preserve existing and concurrent changes: never reset, clean or stash work that is not yours. Never run parallel agents that edit\n  shared modules.\n- When Alex names a step, the test is that step alone through its own harness (extraction: stored requests re-sent, answers sifted,\n  scored against the gold). A full-pipeline run, a registered test, or a paid send beyond the probes of a few cents an agreed direction\n  allows (§7.3) starts only on his explicit word (Alex, 2026-10-27: \"我不是要你看下step 1抽取到底行不行？\").\n- A long paid run is launched detached in a new session with a log and pid file, after checking machine and network health; nothing heavy\n  runs beside paid calls. A gate runs on a snapshot no one is editing.\n- Never open a live run's databases: run `sh <run folder>/snapshot.sh` and query the snapshot.\n- No edit to package code or prompt files while any run is live: the parallel day's manifest hashes every `.py` and prompt file and\n  fails the day. Edit in another worktree or wait.\n- Experiment harnesses send concurrently (a thread pool of 8; the archive is thread-safe); serial sends waste the wall clock Alex is\n  waiting on.\n- **Run settings** (`scripts/replay.py`): extraction requests prepared 16 at a time (`--workers`; the measurement launcher passes its\n  `HIVEMIND_WORKERS` there), Jev matching 8 at a time (`--jev-workers`), judgements 32 at a time (`judging.JUDGE_WORKERS`); a model call\n  times out after 180 s and is tried up to three times.\n  The three draws of a measurement run at once, one launcher each (`docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/harness/run_arm.sh`). Measured\n  timings: `docs/poc/pipeline-plan.md`, \"Run settings and timing\".\n- Report results as they land; scope delegated work so a first useful result returns within 20–30 minutes.\n- Services for testing run on the host (README, \"Run the service for testing\"): on this Mac the VPN gives Docker containers no outbound\n  internet, so a model or embedding call fails inside Docker. Start them with a log and pid file, check them with\n  `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8788/days`, and stop what you started before handing over. Changing Docker or VPN networking is Alex's call.\n- Credentials never appear in Git, documents, logs, prompts, stored data, URLs or command arguments; they are kept in the owner-only file\n  `~/.config/hivemind/credentials.json`, outside the repository. Never raise a spending cap, and never switch a provider or model\n  silently.\n\n## 10. Rebuilding from ../tn-hivemind\n\n- Bring the system over one piece at a time; the product runs end to end at every step.\n- The old code is a source of requirements and stored cases, not a template. Before porting a piece, write what it does, who reads what\n  it writes, and which parts were patches (by their census); port the mechanism, leave the patches. A piece arrives with only the tests\n  that trace to its requirements, and an old rule arrives with the code it governs, as a check where code can hold it.\n\n## 11. Design documents and decisions\n\nThe design is the page `docs/system-design.html` (data in `docs/system-design/new-*.js`), one PRD per module in `docs/prd/` (index\n`README.md`; the extraction standard page sits beside PRD 05) and the decisions. The documents say what the code must do; code that\ndeparts from them waits for a decision.\n\n- The page data is the one source: a PRD block marked `generated` comes from it and is never edited by hand.\n- **Decisions.** `docs/DECISIONS.md` states what is decided now, by module, and gives every decision number's status;\n  `docs/DECISIONS-log.md` holds each decision's full record (Alex's words, what was decided, what was done) and is only appended to. A\n  new decision takes the next number: its record is appended to the log and its entry added to or changed in `docs/DECISIONS.md` in the\n  same change, the entry it replaces marked superseded in the index; the PRD that owns the rule is changed in the same change.\n- After any change, refresh by reasoning: re-read every module in the order and with the four questions of `docs/prd/README.md` (D22), so\n  that page, PRDs and decisions say the same thing, and list each inconsistency fixed. `python3 docs/check.py` runs last and checks only\n  mechanically; its pass is never the refresh.\n- Design every data path from what a view (thesis) needs, never from what the data offers: no number warehouse (D24, D28).\n- Write for a reader who did not follow the discussion: one concrete example, processes as step cards and decisions as trees; every\n  detail page links to its PRD. Maintained documentation, new product text and the pages written for Alex's review are in English (D163;\n  Alex, 2026-11-05: \"不，用英文吧\", D368); source quotations keep their language.\n- A rule is written in full in one place, its owner; summaries, other modules and the glossary name it or point to it without restating\n  its conditions, so a change lands once. A finding that one sentence missed a change is a class: count every place that states the same\n  thing before the first edit (§1).\n- Codex reviews read-only: `codex exec -s read-only -C <repo> --skip-git-repo-check --ephemeral -o <out> - < <prompt>`. The prompt names\n  the scope, the governing documents and what is out of scope; its report is a lead (§1).\n- Before a freeze, review in rounds. Each round runs read-only reviews by angle: an end-to-end simulation of realistic items,\n  state-by-event tables, wording against the glossary, whether an engineer could build each step from the text, every rule against the\n  decisions, an attack on Claude's own findings, a new reader answering questions, every change read in context, and line-by-line reads\n  by module. Each finding is checked against the text before a change; rounds go on until one finds nothing; then the freeze is recorded\n  and the design sealed.\n\n## Before finishing a slice\n\n0. No file of the frozen ruler (§7.1) has changed: `python3 -m pytest tests/test_frozen_rulers.py` is green.\n1. The touched suites, the structural checks and then the full suite pass; for a documents-only change, the reasoning refresh and then\n   `python3 docs/check.py`. A red suite is fixed before a handoff, whoever's code it is.\n2. `docs/CURRENT_STATE.md` holds the status, the open defects and the one next task; a status update retires the paragraphs it replaces.\n   A changed choice is recorded as a decision (§11).\n3. A lesson Alex states is written at the decision it governs in this file, in his words, in the same slice.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^#{1,6} .*D71[12]|''^'\"\\\\| D71[12] ' docs/DECISIONS-log.md docs/DECISIONS.md; rg -n '\"'^#|D71[12]|citation'\"' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | tail -95; rg --files docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^#{1,6} .*D71[12]|''^'\"\\\\| D71[12] ' docs/DECISIONS-log.md docs/DECISIONS.md; rg -n '\"'^#|D71[12]|citation'\"' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | tail -95; rg --files docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design\"","aggregated_output":"docs/DECISIONS.md:1055:| D711 | 2026-11-21 | Pilot pair 1 inconclusive (control-1 double refusal on 09-08: two one-character evidence-id copy errors); the comparison closed, no redraw or resume (council round 37, consensus A). Exploratory beside it: Data Center never above total revenue in linked-1 (control-1 28 of 60 by parser, sampled dates real); four linked CPU double counts in total revenue (H4); H1 at the line (5 against 1). Recommended to Alex: a citation-only judge version with closed per-request id lists, tested at $0; the link direction designed separately | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PILOT-RESULT.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:1056:| D712 | 2026-11-21 | Alex opens a citation-only judge version (\"开引用格式新版本 (推荐)\"): every id field of the judge's answer takes a closed list built from the request; design, council, build, then a $0 test on stored data; any paid test asks Alex again | in force | `docs/DECISIONS-log.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10660:## D711 · 2026-11-21 · Pilot pair 1 is inconclusive (control double refusal); the comparison is closed; council round 37 recommends a citation-only judge version to Alex\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10689:## D712 · 2026-11-21 · Alex opens a citation-only judge version (closed per-request id lists), tested at $0 first\n1:# Current state\n75:Alex has authorized correcting the test-source cleaner and test data when their defects are confirmed, while the frozen production configuration and ruler remain intact. The cleaner switched 615 originally fed articles off; a replay reproduces all 615, and direct inspection confirms an actual article excluded because its 9,874-character body was flattened to one line. Other examples include a wrong-site shell, paywall and long challenge code, so the false-exclusion count and a general article-identification repair remain to be established. The [council regroup](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-REGROUP-COUNCIL.md) and [source-preservation design](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-PRESERVATION-DESIGN.md) describe an isolated candidate checked against all 34,084 records, with a fake-answer actual-runner handoff and provenance display in the replay renderer. The [five source-control calls](../clean-arch/STEP1-CAPTURE-CONTROLS-RESULTS.md) completed and were source-reviewed; two items contain summary details absent from their attached quotations, and one source-visible risk explanation was not returned. This is selected-case evidence, not a general quality result. Broader source-quality comparison, citation completeness and actual writer integration remain open.\n77:**Clean architecture Step 1 (2026-11-06, isolated work on `clean-arch`):** Alex reopened work with the clean architecture. An experimental prepared-source handoff now preserves the archived page, prior cleaned text, source-role decisions and selected-line mapping without changing the original database; quotations for prepared items must also occur contiguously in the original captured page. Two seven-item runs are available in the [clean architecture PRD](../clean-arch/PRD.md), one in the earlier selection order and one in recorded page-timestamp order. The source selector is not a production service and source ordering is not established event-arrival ordering. The runs expose unresolved semantic problems: citations can omit supporting facts despite an exact location match; model output can change a benchmark into a deployment, reverse a backup relation, omit a named customer or assign an unstated currency. A blinded 84-call check-placement/wording comparison and a 27-call same-article citation-completion diagnostic did not give a clean semantic fix and are not adopted. The latter missed an omitted connectivity condition and a reversed backup relationship, and left six expected evidence reviews unaddressed. A further five-round Codex–Claude council produced a narrowly scoped Step 1 link candidate, independently checked for prompt-contract drift. A six-article, 36-call blind comparison completed; the candidate still produced an explicitly self-contradictory link and both arms consistently omitted the same Kyber report and company response. It is not adopted and has not changed the active PRD prompt. A trace confirms that both the Kyber report and open Kyber thesis were supplied, and the raw model answers omitted the report and denial; the reason is not established. See ../poc/data/clean-step1-kyber-trace-2026-11-06/TRACE.md. An isolated six-call comparison showed that hiding the Kyber thesis did not recover the report or denial in any draw. A second six-call comparison returned them in 3/3 draws with the original Kyber paragraph alone and 0/3 with the full article; length, position and surrounding content changed together, so the reason is not isolated. Excerpt outputs have source-attribution limitations. Neither experiment changed state or established a production fix. (Superseded: the next task then was a whole-article coverage approach; the current next task is under \"One next task\".) See ../clean-arch/STEP1-IMPLEMENTATION-COUNCIL.md. The earlier four-round council agreed that no tested semantic fix is ready; its next investigation is a source-backed review of the 49-item historical run and its 160 evidence records, with overlapping issue flags and separate article-level omissions, then a separate comparison of the seven-item replays. See ../clean-arch/STEP1-COUNCIL-REVIEW.md. Preserve relevant evidence while identifying the next intervention; production/frozen history remains as described below. See [Step 1 run log](../clean-arch/STEP1-RUN-LOG.md) and [English reading page](../clean-arch/architecture.html).\n103:## Future evidence scoring (D372)\n107:## Latest decision (D369)\n124:**Clean Step 1 fidelity review (2026-11-07):** All 49 saved source packets and 160 original evidence items have received a source-and-record review; focused independent cross-checks cover the findings and selected controls. The [review and article replay](../clean-arch/STEP1-FIDELITY-REVIEW.md) distinguish source contamination and missing source material from model meaning, citation, date and link issues. The [isolated schema property-order diagnostic](../clean-arch/STEP1-CITATION-ORDER-RESULTS.md) completed all 66 calls and condition-blinded article reviews. Several omissions and semantic errors persisted; it did not establish a fix and is not adopted. It used saved articles and before-states without changing production.\n128:## What runs\n140:## Open defects\n159:## One next task\n448:**The one next task (D711, 2026-11-21): Alex's choice on opening a citation-only judge version** (closed per-request id lists in the\n451:- **Verdict:** inconclusive (D711). control-1 stopped on 09-08 on a double refusal: two one-character evidence-id copy errors. linked-1\n459:  - the citation-only version is the recommendation;\n492:  passed review; the pilot ran at $1.70 and is inconclusive (D710, D711).\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/codex-r3.stream\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/mutants.log\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/rebuild-control.log\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/claude-marks.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/codex-r10.stream\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/round4-brief.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/round5-brief.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/filing-exposure.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/blind-reader-brief.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/codex-r12.stream\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/linked-v9-0710-request.txt\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/codex-r1.stream\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/brief.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/rebuild_control.py\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/claude-r1.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/codex-r1.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/send-stdout.log\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/round10-brief.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/round11-brief.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/codex-r12.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/codex-r5.stream\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/codex-r5.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/codex-r9.stream\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/round9-brief.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/round8-brief.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/codex-r4.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/codex-r7.stream\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/selection_census.py\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/round3-brief.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/round2-brief.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-d