{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '287,440p'; rg -n 'JudgementRefused|judging_failed|run_rejudging' src/hivemind scripts\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '287,440p'; rg -n 'JudgementRefused|judging_failed|run_rejudging' src/hivemind scripts\"","aggregated_output":"   287\tdef queued_by_change(conn, view_id):\n   288\t    \"\"\"What a changed conclusion of this view queues: its dependants and, for a theme thesis, every open asset thesis. The one rule,\n   289\t    read for a live judgement and for the judgements a resumed round finds committed.\"\"\"\n   290\t    queued = store.dependants_of(conn, view_id)\n   291\t    if store.view(conn, view_id)['object_kind'] == 'theme':\n   292\t        queued = queued + open_asset_views(conn)\n   293\t    return queued\n   294\t\n   295\t\n   296\tdef queued_by_ledger(conn, seq):\n   297\t    \"\"\"What the judgements already committed at this sequence number queued; a fresh round finds nothing here, a resumed round\n   298\t    finds what the interrupted one had queued in memory.\"\"\"\n   299\t    queued = []\n   300\t    for row in conn.execute('select view_id from judgements where seq=? and changed=1 order by judgement_id', (seq,)):\n   301\t        queued.extend(queued_by_change(conn, row['view_id']))\n   302\t    return queued\n   303\t\n   304\t\n   305\tdef round_of_judgements(archive, cfg, conn, changed_views, seq, item, *, transport=None):\n   306\t    \"\"\"Judge the open views in changed_views, dependencies first; a changed conclusion queues open dependants.\n   307\t\n   308\t    Views that do not depend on each other are judged at the same time: each level of the dependency order is sent\n   309\t    to the model concurrently (the prompts are built and the answers checked and written in this thread, so the\n   310\t    database connection never crosses threads). A view waits while anything upstream of it is still pending, so a\n   311\t    dependant always reads this round's conclusion of its dependency. A view with no evidence in force stays\n   312\t    unjudged (D59), and a view already judged at this sequence number (a resumed round) is not judged twice.\n   313\t\n   314\t    Among the views ready to be judged, theme theses go first, so an asset thesis reads this round's theme conclusions; a theme judgement that says changed queues every open asset thesis with\n   315\t    evidence in force. The starting queue adds what the ledger says earlier commits at this sequence number queued.\"\"\"\n   316\t    import concurrent.futures\n   317\t\n   318\t    version = cfg.rejudging.prompt_version\n   319\t    schema = schema_for(version)\n   320\t\n   321\t    def eligible(view_id):\n   322\t        return store.is_open(conn, view_id) and not store.has_judgement(conn, view_id, seq) and bool(store.evidence_in_force(conn, view_id))\n   323\t\n   324\t    def is_theme(view_id):\n   325\t        return store.view(conn, view_id)['object_kind'] == 'theme'\n   326\t\n   327\t    pending = [v for v in topological(conn, list(changed_views) + queued_by_ledger(conn, seq)) if eligible(v)]\n   328\t    done, results = set(), []\n   329\t    while pending:\n   330\t        ready = [v for v in pending if upstream(conn, v).isdisjoint(set(pending) - {v})] or pending[:1]\n   331\t        level = [v for v in ready if is_theme(v)] or ready\n   332\t        prompts = {v: build_prompt(conn, v, version) for v in level}\n   333\t\n   334\t        def ask(view_id, note=''):\n   335\t            system, user = prompts[view_id]\n   336\t            return model.call(archive, cfg, cfg.rejudging, system, user + note, schema, 'judgement', 'judge', transport=transport)\n   337\t\n   338\t        with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=JUDGE_WORKERS) as pool_:\n   339\t            answers = dict(zip(level, pool_.map(ask, level)))\n   340\t        for view_id in level:\n   341\t            answer = answers[view_id]\n   342\t            errors = check_answer(conn, view_id, answer.data, prompts[view_id][1])\n   343\t            if errors:\n   344\t                archive.retire(answer.call_id)                 # a refused answer never answers the same request again (a resume re-samples)\n   345\t                answer = ask(view_id, retry_note(errors))\n   346\t                errors = check_answer(conn, view_id, answer.data, prompts[view_id][1])\n   347\t                if errors:\n   348\t                    archive.retire(answer.call_id)\n   349\t                    raise JudgementRefused(f'{view_id}: ' + '; '.join(errors))\n   350\t            result = _record(conn, cfg, view_id, seq, item, answer)\n   351\t            done.add(view_id)\n   352\t            results.append(result)\n   353\t            if result['changed']:\n   354\t                for dependant in queued_by_change(conn, view_id):\n   355\t                    if dependant not in done and dependant not in pending and eligible(dependant):\n   356\t                        pending.append(dependant)\n   357\t        pending = [v for v in topological(conn, pending) if v not in done and eligible(v)]\n   358\t    return results\nsrc/hivemind/views/round.py:90:    except judging.JudgementRefused as error:\nsrc/hivemind/views/round.py:93:        return _fail(conn, marker, seq, result, 'judged', 'judging_failed', 'judging: ' + repr(error), type(error).__name__)\nsrc/hivemind/views/judging.py:99:class JudgementRefused(Exception):\nsrc/hivemind/views/judging.py:349:                    raise JudgementRefused(f'{view_id}: ' + '; '.join(errors))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'p=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad; cat \"$p/enum_size_census.py\" \"$p/id_typo_census.py\"; ls poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-{1,2,3}/prod \"$p/control-1-copy\" \"$p/linked-1-copy\"; which claude; rg -n '\"'openai|gpt-' poc/config/poc-v118.json; rg -n 'D198 |D354 |D359 |D694 ' docs/DECISIONS.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'p=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad; cat \"$p/enum_size_census.py\" \"$p/id_typo_census.py\"; ls poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-{1,2,3}/prod \"$p/control-1-copy\" \"$p/linked-1-copy\"; which claude; rg -n '\"'openai|gpt-' poc/config/poc-v118.json; rg -n 'D198 |D354 |D359 |D694 ' docs/DECISIONS.md\"","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"Per stored judge request: how many ids each closed list would hold (evidence shown, dependencies listed, themes shown) and their chars.\"\"\"\nimport sqlite3, json, re, sys\nsys.path.insert(0, '/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src')\nfrom hivemind.views import judging\ndef deps_in(u):\n    p = u.split('\\n[Current conclusions of the theses it depends on]', 1)\n    return re.findall(r'^- (v\\d+) \\(', p[1].split('\\n\\n[', 1)[0], re.M) if len(p) == 2 else []\nfor label, path, MIN in [(a.split(\"|\")[0], a.split(\"|\")[1], int(a.split(\"|\")[2])) for a in sys.argv[1:]]:\n    a = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{path}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    n = 0; worst = (0,); totals = []\n    for cid, req in a.execute(\"select call_id, request_json from model_calls where purpose='judge' and call_id>?\", (MIN,)):\n        u = json.loads(req)['messages'][-1]['content']\n        e, t, d = judging.evidence_shown_in(u), judging.themes_shown_in(u), deps_in(u)\n        total = 2 * len(e) + len(t) + len(d)          # evidence ids in cites and in push ids\n        chars = sum(len(x) for x in e)\n        totals.append(total); n += 1\n        if total > worst[0]: worst = (total, cid, len(e), len(t), len(d), chars)\n    totals.sort()\n    print(f'{label}: {n} judge requests; enum values per request median {totals[len(totals)//2]}, p99 {totals[int(len(totals)*0.99)]}, max {worst[0]} '\n          f'(call {worst[1]}: evidence {worst[2]}, themes {worst[3]}, deps {worst[4]}, evidence id chars {worst[5]}); over 500: {sum(t > 500 for t in totals)}')\n\"\"\"Census of refused judge answers on stored v118 runs: which are evidence-id copy errors (one edit from a shown id).\"\"\"\nimport sqlite3, json, re, sys\ndef edits1(a, b):\n    if a == b: return False\n    if abs(len(a) - len(b)) > 1: return False\n    if len(a) == len(b): return sum(x != y for x, y in zip(a, b)) == 1\n    s, l = (a, b) if len(a) < len(b) else (b, a)\n    return any(l[:i] + l[i+1:] == s for i in range(len(l)))\ndef shown(u):\n    p = u.split('\\n[Evidence in ', 1)\n    return re.findall(r'^- (e\\d+) \\[', p[1].split('\\n\\n[', 1)[0], re.M) if len(p) == 2 else []\nfor label, path, min_call in [(x.split('|')[0], x.split('|')[1], int(x.split('|')[2])) for x in sys.argv[1:]]:\n    a = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{path}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    total = a.execute(\"select count(*) from model_calls where purpose='judge' and call_id>?\", (min_call,)).fetchone()[0]\n    rows = a.execute(\"select call_id, request_json, answer_json from model_calls where purpose='judge' and call_id>? and request_sha256 like '%:refused:%'\", (min_call,)).fetchall()\n    classes = {}\n    retries = 0\n    for cid, req, ans in rows:\n        u = json.loads(req)['messages'][-1]['content']\n        if 'The code returned the previous answer because' in u: retries += 1\n        ids = shown(u)\n        try: d = json.loads(ans)\n        except Exception: classes.setdefault('unparsed', []).append(cid); continue\n        bad = sorted({c for c in d.get('cites', [])} | {p['evidence_id'] for p in d.get('pushes', [])} - set(ids)) if ids else []\n        bad = [b for b in bad if b not in ids]\n        if not bad: cls = 'other check (not an evidence id)'\n        elif all(any(edits1(b, s) for s in ids) for b in bad): cls = 'id one edit from a shown id'\n        else: cls = 'id not near any shown id'\n        classes.setdefault(cls, []).append((cid, bad[:3]))\n    print(f'{label}: judge calls {total}, refused {len(rows)} (of which retry answers {retries})')\n    for k, v in classes.items(): print('   ', k, len(v), v[:6])\n/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/control-1-copy:\narchive.sqlite\nsnapshots.jsonl\nsummary.json\nviews.sqlite\n\n/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/linked-1-copy:\narchive.sqlite\nsnapshots.jsonl\nsummary.json\nviews.sqlite\n\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod:\narchive.sqlite\nmanifests\nreplay.log\nviews.sqlite\n\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod:\narchive.sqlite\nmanifests\nreplay.log\nviews.sqlite\n\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-3/prod:\narchive.sqlite\nmanifests\nreplay.log\nviews.sqlite\n/opt/homebrew/bin/claude\n4:  \"provider\": \"openai\",\n8:      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n14:      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n20:      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n26:      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n32:      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n38:      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n44:      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n50:      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n56:      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n62:      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n76:    \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n82:    \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n88:    \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n94:    \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n542:| D198 | 2026-10-27 | A judgement reads the evidence in view, not everything in force | in force | §7 Thesis library |\n698:| D354 | 2026-11-03 | Steps 3 and 4 (opening and matching questions, judging them) are frozen as `poc-v108` runs them, after thre… | in force (amended by D359) | §7 Thesis library |\n703:| D359 | 2026-11-04 | The code builds only the frozen prompts (extraction v74i, judging-v7); old worktrees removed; the preflight… | in force (amended by D364, D365) | §6 Extraction |\n1033:| D689 | 2026-11-20 | Alex chooses option 1: poc-v118 stays production, the hybrid's release line is paused, the release bar unchanged; council N (fresh Codex thread, consensus) closes the judge line and the c8 reading line for now under D543, D198 unchanged, nothing sent; reopening: judge on eight eligible failures on fresh questions plus matched controls and a source-checked summary (D198 option 2), then Alex's choice and funding; c8 on a traced decisive fact it delivers that old missed; D439 accounting error recorded ($39.65–$44.42 under two readings; $0 available without Alex) | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-n-codex.md` |\n1038:| D694 | 2026-11-21 | Alex chooses A: a chosen reading link leaves filing alone (D265 applies only to a stated hierarchy); new matching and judging versions open for linking (both opening orders); the July comparison (cap $0.15) after the council passes the $0 proof; the sourced reference not opened | in force | `docs/DECISIONS-log.md` |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
