{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'cap|input|enum' docs/research/2026-10-27-evidence-in-view/design.md | head -25; rg -n 'e3111|e3620|e88' docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PILOT-RESULT.md docs/DECISIONS-log.md | tail -10; sed -n '141,165p' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md\"","aggregated_output":"10:enumerating 300+ ids. Two mechanisms, each at its own writer (census: `census.py`, this folder):\n92:stay unjudged) — eligibility unchanged. 06-views step 7 \"rejudge only open theses whose inputs changed\" — triggers unchanged;\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PILOT-RESULT.md:10:  - Call 8938 cited `e362` for `e3620`.\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PILOT-RESULT.md:11:  - The retry, call 8941, cited `e3111`, one character from `e3110` and `e3112`.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:9235:  - Both independent reviews of design version 1 found the conflict: the Codex review (thread 01a1ebb0-9724-7e51-a979-bae88cb9cba9) and the\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10664:  the listed evidence (`e362` for `e3620`; `e3111` beside `e3110`/`e3112`), PAID-DESIGN.md §4 (2). linked-1 completed with every\n\n1. **Competitor and customer news is filed under the company's revenue questions** instead of the share, capital-spending or custom-chip question it informs (D355; filing is otherwise about 85% right). Share facts are often not written at all, an extraction recall miss. The total-revenue question holds about a quarter of all links (D354).\n2. **One bet opened twice** about one encounter in five: the collision judge splits a seed question from an identical candidate on a fine detail (D354).\n3. **A question the standard rules out** (the lidar legislation) was proposed by the extraction and opened in one draw of three (D354).\n4. **A thesis opened from an article gets no dependency of its own**: the default Jev matching asks for none (`views/jev_matching.py`), although D51 has the matching call choose them; themes still reach every company thesis through the theme block (D191, D195). Found in the 2026-11-05 consolidation; building it is decided (D368).\n5. **Historical coverage-start reading, retired by D370** (D364–D366): the capital-spending line is missed in about one read in six (the question is then left as it was); a labelled guidance figure is written with the fact tier; later reports reach the questions only through the daily stream; `scripts/preflight.py` does not replay the reading's check.\n6. **Measured on one company and one 14-day window**, the judgement scored at the window end only; no version of the current pipeline has completed a longer window (a 60-day run of `poc-v108` was stopped at Alex's word after 2026-07-15, [log row 8](research/2026-11-04-argument-record/log.md)). The China-share question (v17) swings between draws (0 of 3 in the acceptance, 2 of 3 in its control, 1 of 3 in the frozen draws): two readers found the starting figures did not cause the acceptance's drop, and the byte-identical extraction request kept a \"share fell to zero\" sentence in two candidate draws and dropped it in two control draws. One acceptance draw judged nothing on v16; its cause is not established.\n7. **What a judgement reads grows with the window** (D358). Argument records (D201) were measured as the remedy on 2026-11-04 and not built: judging-v8 agreed 12 of 17 against 15 of 17, judging-v9's card added little at about half again the judging cost; their code was removed at Alex's request ([log rows 4–11](research/2026-11-04-argument-record/log.md)).\n8. **Seen once, not traced.** A judgement named a shown theme as a dependency and the check refused it twice, stopping a draw for a day (2026-11-02, D266). The sealed run's review recorded that a succession's opening evidence is not linked to the new question (D358), not yet checked against today's code.\n9. **Earlier defects, unchanged.** Matching (build log row 49): another document's copy of a figure can be treated as new evidence; one matter can occupy several groups; same-answer candidate references caused seven chain or duplication decisions of the generative matcher; empty `original_who` values can count as the same party; different names for one population cause two of nine Jev merge misses. Nine 2026 aggregate-spending theses under `ai-capex` each have a different population; whether to combine them is a product choice. Extraction's instructions remain narrower than the PRD's important-question rule and omit the personal-memo exception, and extraction can change a quantity's meaning before matching (a guarantee amount against financing provided). Classification keeps its [recorded simulation defects](research/2026-10-25-english/classification-existing-defects.txt). The corpus audit recorded 97 official notices with 56 body and file-name collisions, to re-fetch before relying on a rebuilt corpus. An older intermittent search-test failure is untraced. Fresh Idea allocations vary while saved weights do not; the confidence chart applies the current plan to past states and is not a calibrated probability; broad analyst-prose quality and fresh Idea stability remain unaccepted (the [Idea contract](poc/idea-card.md) lists its limits); generative matching dependencies await `matching-v4`. The readers' doubts about the frozen standard, listed in the [extraction branch's state page](research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/current-state-extraction-branch-2026-11-03.md), remain for Alex.\n\nUpstream supply and the human review pool's output remain deferred.\n\n10. **A new-system store being written serves its first day in progress** (D573, D574; `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/page-contract/LIVE-READ-DESIGN.md`, B):\n   before any day completes, the service's default date falls back to the latest judgement's day. Not built: a correct guard needs one\n   snapshot for the check and the read, MCP's start and the streamed Idea response handled; 0 of 143 stores are in that state and no\n   new-system store is served live today.\n\n## One next task\n\n**Where the lean path stands (2026-11-15; D489 to D542).** Alex is not active (D509); D439 is in force: choices go to the\ncouncil (an independent Codex review and Claude) until consensus, recorded citing D439; nothing is pushed, deployed, published or\ncommitted; paid calls stay within D439's $40 ceiling (about $18.42 recorded; $0.0134 sent in this period, the ten judge calls of\nD511 and D519; the lean path $8.34 in all). Every stretch below is closed; its full record is in the decision log and in\n`research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md` (sections 1 to 43).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '3763,3797p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-04-argument-record/predictions-step2b.md | head -17; nl -ba clean-arch/e2e-misses-2026-11-11/resend.py | sed -n '119,139p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/probe.py | sed -n '50,71p'\"","aggregated_output":"## D357 · 2026-11-04 · Clean the repository of configurations and prompts nothing current names; the code paths of retired versions are a slice of their own\n\n- Alex, with D356: \"然后你也需要清理repo不要让旧的东西影响我们整个sanity\".\n- Removed (Git keeps them): 53 configurations under `poc/config/` and 87 prompt files under `src/hivemind/prompts/` that no test, code,\n  script, Docker file, README, AGENTS, state page, PRD, POC plan, design page or skill names, and that no kept configuration uses. Kept:\n  every configuration those name (54, among them the replay default `poc-v108`, the service's `poc-v33-idea` and the stored controls\n  `poc-v94`, `poc-v95`, `poc-v103` of D274) and every prompt file a kept configuration or a test, code or script names (112). Two files the\n  first pass missed were put back because a test reads them by a computed name (`categories-v7.json`, `role-v7.txt`); the full suite then\n  passed (288), with the frozen-file tests, the UI tests and `docs/check.py`.\n- Stale text removed from the current documents: the final-verdict draft (D356), the README's pre-merge extraction status (role-v51 and a\n  placement call), and the pull-mode open items D356 settled.\n- Worktrees: the two that held no changes and no data (`fix/question-identity-r2`, `cleanup/stale-tests-20261026`) were removed; their\n  branches stay. Left for Alex because they hold uncommitted changes or local data: `feat/thesis-admission-v12` (7 changed files, 1\n  untracked), `feat/parallel-day` (2 changed files), `fix/thesis-admission-v11` (102 MB of local run data), `cleanup/sequential-requests`\n  (685 MB of local run data, 1 untracked file), `fix/extraction-quality-2026-10-28` (the stored runs of the end-to-end loop that later\n  scripts read).\n- Not done in this slice: the code paths that only retired prompt versions take (version gates in `extraction.py` and `views/judging.py`)\n  and the tests that load old configurations to reach them (22 test files). Removing them is a refactor of its own, proved against the\n  frozen request bytes (`tests/test_frozen_extraction_prompt.py`); it waits for Alex to take it up.\n\n## D358 · 2026-10-28 (carried 2026-11-04) · The three-month run stops at 2026-08-28 and is sealed; evidence bloat is the next problem to solve\n\nRecorded on 2026-10-28 as D206 of `feat/thesis-admission-v12` in that worktree's uncommitted decision log, and never merged; carried into\n`main` on 2026-11-04 when the worktree was removed (D359), its text unchanged below. Its D206 is a different decision on `main`.\nIts quality review is carried as `docs/research/2026-10-28-quality-review/` (documents and scripts; the comparison databases stay in\nthe backup). The writer fix it names was not carried: `main` reads cited ids as a set where it serves them (`bundle.library`,\n`service`), which covers the same defect. The succession gap it records was not checked against today's code.\n\n- Alex, 16:30: \"你先停止吧，把这个db 封存，替换成最新的FE可以读取然后把这个 bloating evidence 的问题给记录下来，很严重，需要解决\". Earlier (16:12): \"证据膨胀是一个问题，我们之后要想办法deal\".\n- The run (`english-v34-nvda-3m-2026-10-28`, poc-v34, the D202–D205 writer) completed 59 days, 2026-07-01 to 08-28: 1,232 items, 69 theses, 7,091 calls, $5.80. It is sealed read-only as `poc/data/sealed-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/` (SQLite online backups, SHA256SUMS, logs and scripts; the run folder is left resumable). The front end reads it from 16:35: the served defaults switched in the five places the README names (main checkout), `poc/mock/index.html` rebuilt, the API restarted in `service-3m-2026-10-28/` (`/days` 2026-07-01..08-28, 69 theses).\n- Why it stops: evidence bloat. The Data Center revenue thesis (v10) carried 1,768 linked pieces by 08-27 and FY2027 revenue (v2) 1,733; v10's judging request was 292 KB with 698 evidence ids shown; the model mislabels one id among dozens of pushes about every other attempt, the code refuses the answer, two refusals halt the day. Today: 14 judge answers refused by code, 10 on v10/v2/v13, two days halted on v10 alone in 16:05–16:21. Of 25 pieces linked to v2, 10 bear on the question (Claude's reading); the judge ever cited 23–27% of what is linked. The census, the one-case traces and the rule candidates are in `docs/research/2026-10-28-quality-review/report.md` §2 D (and A–C, measured first); the step is Alex's to pick.\n- Found while switching the front end: one judgement (v2, id 736) cited an id twice and the UI contract (`thesis-ui/2`, uniqueItems) refused the dataset. The writer now stores each cited id once (`judging._record`, test `test_a_judgement_stores_each_cited_id_once`, red on the old writer); the two readers of sealed ledgers (`bundle.library`, `service` thesis bundles, main checkout) read the set, since a sealed ledger does not change.\n- The other halts of the day, each resumed by the run's `watch.sh` and recorded in the cost ledger: the judging output cap (D205), the Mac sleeping, three transport errors, one \"database is locked\" (a reader held the ledger over the 5 s busy timeout), one hung call (55 min at 0% CPU under the VPN; a stall detector was added to the watcher).\n- Amendment, 17:05. Alex, on seeing an empty thesis in the front end (\"why is this here? there is no evidence and why is this a thesis\"; then \"你直接把它移除，这是我们自己的失误\"): v68, \"What stand-alone CPU revenue will NVIDIA report for calendar 2027?\", opened on the run's last day by the succession rule (D168: same quantity, next period, after v24) from one statement (\"$20 billion in 2026 and more than $40 billion in 2027\"); the writer linked that statement to v7 and v24 (as a repeat of the $20 billion piece) and not to the successor it opened, so v68 stood with no evidence and, judging running only on arrivals, no judgement. Class: 1 of 69 theses with no evidence; 1 of 2 successions (v9 after v8 has 59 pieces). The sealed folder stays untouched; the front end, the API and the page build now read `poc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite`, the same ledger with v68's rows removed (views, view_keys, rungs, successions, view_switches, views_fts; the append-only triggers dropped in that copy only; its README lists this). The writer gap (a succession's opening evidence is not linked to the successor) is an open defect in `writing.py` for the next slice.\n\n     1\t# 第 2 步重跑（judging-v9）预期：发送前写下并冻结，2026-11-04\n     2\t\n     3\t运行：`poc-v110`（`poc-v108` 只把判断换成 judging-v9：v7 的读法、上一次结论和答题项，加一张每次照写、下次不读回的论证卡片），一遍，2026-07-01 到 07-14，\n     4\tNVDA，22 道种子题。存档以冻结版 v108 第 1 遍的存档起步：抽取、开题、匹配用存下的回答，只有判断是新的。合格线全部取自 `targets.md`（sha256 c9dc858d…），\n     5\t不新加。这是一遍：能看出机制，不能单凭它说两个版本谁好；T1 的\"三遍都对的题一道不丢\"要第 3 步的三遍才能判。\n     6\t\n     7\t| # | 目标（targets.md） | 预期 | 停下的条件 |\n     8\t|---|---|---|---|\n     9\t| T1 | 判断准 | 冻结尺子 7-14：不低于 15/17；总收入、数据中心收入两题判对（几美分的检查里 6/6）；融资承诺可能落在第 3 档（v7 自己在这天也是一半一半，几美分的检查里 5/6 判对） | 14/17 或更低 |\n    10\t| T2 | 不被上一次的想法绑住 | 以前判断用过、仍然有效、最后不再给看的报道：不多于 v7 的 7 条（读法和 v7 相同，预期相近） | 多于 15 条 |\n    11\t| T3a | 理由有出处 | 写进库里的卡片：理由里有引用没写的数字 0 条（代码在写入前拒收） | 大于 0 |\n    12\t| T3b | 来源数算对 | 独立来源数大于\"引用数减转载数\"的理由 0 条（代码拒收） | 大于 0 |\n    13\t| T3c | 卡片讲的对 | 跑完后读者读 10 张卡片，并读同 10 题 v7 的理由作对照；我逐条核实 | 核实后实质错误多于 v7 理由 |\n    14\t| T4 | 跑得稳 | 0 天停下；退回两次 0；第一次回答被退回不超过 15%（几美分的检查里 6.3%） | 有一天停下 |\n    15\t| — | 成本 | 判断约 0.6～0.7 美元（输入同 v7，输出同 v8，估计值）；只记录 | 整遍超过 3 美元上限（运行会自己停） |\n   119\t    saved = saved_judgement(draw, view, day) if which == 'accepted' else saved_first_request(draw, view, day)\n   120\t    requests = json.loads((DATA / f'control-d{draw}' / 'control-requests.json').read_text())\n   121\t    report = json.loads((DATA / f'control-d{draw}' / 'control-report.json').read_text())\n   122\t    if not report['passed'] or report['saved run'] != str(edge_replay.SAVED):\n   123\t        raise SystemExit(f'the offline replay of draw {draw} did not pass or is of another run')\n   124\t    request = requests.get(saved['request_sha256'])\n   125\t    if request is None:\n   126\t        raise SystemExit(f'the replay of draw {draw} holds no request {saved[\"request_sha256\"]}')\n   127\t    canonical = json.dumps(request, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False)\n   128\t    if canonical != saved['request_json'] or sha256(canonical) != saved['request_sha256']:\n   129\t        raise SystemExit(f'draw {draw} {view} {day}: the rebuilt request is not the saved one')\n   130\t    cfg = config.load(edge_replay.e2e_adapter.CONFIG)\n   131\t    rebuilt = model.build_request(cfg.rejudging, request['messages'][0]['content'], request['messages'][-1]['content'],\n   132\t                                  judging.schema_for(cfg.rejudging.prompt_version), 'judgement', cfg.provider)\n   133\t    if json.dumps(rebuilt) != json.dumps(request):\n   134\t        raise SystemExit(f'draw {draw} {view} {day}: the request is not, byte for byte, what model.build_request builds today')\n   135\t    ledger = ledger_before(draw, day)\n   136\t    with contextlib.closing(read_only(ledger)) as conn:\n   137\t        if conn.execute('select 1 from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day=?', (view, day)).fetchone():\n   138\t            raise SystemExit(f'the ledger before {day} already holds that day\\'s judgement of {view}')\n   139\t        user = request['messages'][-1]['content']\n    50\t        copy.execute(\"insert into dependencies(view_id, depends_on, wait_chain_view_id, wait_year, direction, seq) values (?, ?, '', '', 'first_is_bullish', ?)\",\n    51\t                     (data_center, total, last['seq']))\n    52\t    copy.commit()\n    53\t    return copy, dict(last)\n    54\t\n    55\t\n    56\tdef requests(scratch):\n    57\t    cfg = config.load(str(REPO / 'poc/config/poc-v118.json'))\n    58\t    version = cfg.rejudging.prompt_version\n    59\t    schema = judging.schema_for(version)\n    60\t    out = {}\n    61\t    for draw, (data_center, total) in PAIRS.items():\n    62\t        for arm in ('control', 'changed'):\n    63\t            conn, last = prepared(scratch, draw, arm == 'changed')\n    64\t            system, user = judging.build_prompt(conn, data_center, version)\n    65\t            request = model.build_request(cfg.rejudging, system, user, schema, 'judgement', cfg.provider)\n    66\t            _, sha = model.request_identity(request)\n    67\t            out[(draw, arm)] = {'conn': conn, 'system': system, 'user': user, 'sha': sha, 'stored_sha': last['request_sha256'],\n    68\t                                'day': last['publication_day'], 'seq': last['seq']}\n    69\t    return cfg, schema, out\n    70\t\n    71\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
