{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 PYTHONPATH=src python3 -c '\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport sqlite3,json,collections,re\nfrom hivemind.views import judging\np=Path('\\\\''poc/data/sealed-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/archive.sqlite'\\\\'').resolve()\na=sqlite3.connect(f'\\\\''file:{p}?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'',uri=True)\ncount=collections.Counter(); rows=[]\nfor cid,req in a.execute(\\\"select call_id,request_json from model_calls where purpose='\\\\''judge'\\\\''\\\"):\n u=json.loads(req)['\\\\''messages'\\\\''][-1]['\\\\''content'\\\\'']\n e=judging.evidence_shown_in(u)\n if len(e)>0:\n  t=judging.themes_shown_in(u)\n  count['\\\\''current format matches'\\\\'']+=1\n  header='\\\\''\\\\n[Current conclusions of the theses it depends on]'\\\\''\n  deps=set(re.findall(r'\\\\''\"'^- (v'\"\\\\d+) \\\\('\\\\'',u.split(header,1)[1].split('\\\\''\\\\n\\\\n['\\\\'',1)[0],re.M)) if header in u else set()\n  total=2*len(e)+len(t)+len(deps)+6\n  count['\\\\''plain over 1000'\\\\'']+=int(total>1000)\n  count['\\\\''shared over 1000 if counted once'\\\\'']+=int(len(e)+len(t)+len(deps)+6>1000)\n  rows.append((total,cid,u.split()[1],len(e),len(t),len(deps)))\n else:\n  count['\\\\''other (or empty)'\\\\'']+=1\nprint(dict(count), sorted(rows,reverse=True)[:5])\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 PYTHONPATH=src python3 -c '\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport sqlite3,json,collections,re\nfrom hivemind.views import judging\np=Path('\\\\''poc/data/sealed-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/archive.sqlite'\\\\'').resolve()\na=sqlite3.connect(f'\\\\''file:{p}?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'',uri=True)\ncount=collections.Counter(); rows=[]\nfor cid,req in a.execute(\\\"select call_id,request_json from model_calls where purpose='\\\\''judge'\\\\''\\\"):\n u=json.loads(req)['\\\\''messages'\\\\''][-1]['\\\\''content'\\\\'']\n e=judging.evidence_shown_in(u)\n if len(e)>0:\n  t=judging.themes_shown_in(u)\n  count['\\\\''current format matches'\\\\'']+=1\n  header='\\\\''\\\\n[Current conclusions of the theses it depends on]'\\\\''\n  deps=set(re.findall(r'\\\\''\"'^- (v'\"\\\\d+) \\\\('\\\\'',u.split(header,1)[1].split('\\\\''\\\\n\\\\n['\\\\'',1)[0],re.M)) if header in u else set()\n  total=2*len(e)+len(t)+len(deps)+6\n  count['\\\\''plain over 1000'\\\\'']+=int(total>1000)\n  count['\\\\''shared over 1000 if counted once'\\\\'']+=int(len(e)+len(t)+len(deps)+6>1000)\n  rows.append((total,cid,u.split()[1],len(e),len(t),len(deps)))\n else:\n  count['\\\\''other (or empty)'\\\\'']+=1\nprint(dict(count), sorted(rows,reverse=True)[:5])\n'\"","aggregated_output":"{'current format matches': 949, 'plain over 1000': 10, 'shared over 1000 if counted once': 0} [(1323, 6918, 'v2', 647, 23, 0), (1207, 6960, 'v10', 589, 23, 0), (1207, 6959, 'v10', 589, 23, 0), (1207, 6915, 'v10', 589, 23, 0), (1171, 6507, 'v2', 571, 23, 0)]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"agent_message","text":"**Round 38 verdict: revise the design before coding.** Old-2’s first bad citation, `e88`, shows why. I fed the saved answer through the real `model.call` with the proposed list. It raised `SchemaError` before the judge’s retry could run. T1 currently requires both that rejection and the old retry to happen in the same replay. [Old-2 archive](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/archive.sqlite) · [Answer validation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:251) · [Judge retry](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:334)\n\n1. **The tables need corrections.** A format-invalid answer is saved as `:schema:` and takes the `judging_failed` path. Two refusals by `check_answer` take the distinct `judgement_refused_twice` path. If one worker raises a format error, other workers in that batch can already have saved answers even though that batch writes no judgements. On resume, committed judgements are skipped and saved answers can be reused when the rebuilt request matches. A changed config or changed inputs can produce a different request. The old-check table also omits duplicate theme pushes, which still trigger the existing retry even when every ID is allowed. The reader table misses a concrete gap: preflight checks refused judge answers against the fixed v7 format, and its stored-record replay covers matching. It would miss a new citation-format error unless it reads the format saved with that call. [Design tables](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/DESIGN.md:89) · [Judge checks and workers](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:215) · [Day failure handling](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/round.py:73) · [Preflight](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/preflight.py:59)\n\n2. **Plain enums are safest for the five supplied archives. A shared enum is the candidate for the larger requests already seen.** I reproduced a maximum of **915 values** across all fields, **2,237 characters** in the largest individual enum, and **4,659 characters** under the provider’s total-string rule. But in the sealed D358 archive, **10 of 949** stored judge requests would exceed 1,000 values with plain enums. Call 6918 has 647 evidence IDs and would need **1,323 values**, or **676** if a shared evidence enum counts once. First verify the actual outgoing format against that call and an empty list. OpenAI documents references and `maxItems`, but does not specify how repeated references count. A pattern has another exactness problem: the local validator uses `re.search`, and a conventional `$` ending can accept a trailing newline. Provider acceptance of the exact format remains unverified. [D358](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:3785) · [Sealed archive](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/sealed-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/archive.sqlite) · [Local validator](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:184) · [OpenAI Structured Outputs limits](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/structured-outputs#supported-schemas)\n\n3. **Build the lists from the exact rows used to render the request. Use the saved text when reviewing archived calls.** In both v7 and v8, each resolved dependency gets a numbered entry, even if it is closed or has never been judged. A waiting dependency gets a sentence with no citable target. That makes the rendered IDs equal to `check_answer`’s dependency IDs **at the same store state**. I found no discrepancy in the supplied archives, including 268 fresh linked requests with a dependency block. I reproduced two counterexamples in memory. After a waiting dependency resolves to `v4`, a later check allows `v4` against the older request that never listed it. And the proposed line parser mistook a line in a v7 dependency’s reasons for a second dependency. v8 indents those reasons, but a multiline evidence quote fooled the existing evidence parser in both versions. Taking the IDs from the same rows that render the request avoids granting an ID merely because it appeared inside a quote or explanation. [Renderer and text readers](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:122) · [Dependency lookup](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/store.py:242) · [Waiting-dependency writer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/writing.py:50)\n\n4. **Use one fresh judge version name. Defer the v8-based product version.** The name gives the existing config, support check and frozen tests one way to select the contract. A flag would add another combination to validate. `judging-v9` already named the argument-card experiment in `poc-v110`, so choose an unused name. The shared format builder can prove nonempty dependency lists against the saved v8 requests offline, without adding a second runnable version. [Config loader](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/config.py:20) · [Frozen tests](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_frozen_questions_and_judgement.py:14) · [Earlier judging-v9](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-04-argument-record/predictions-step2b.md:1)\n\n5. **Reuse the replay runner and change the proof.** The current harness looks up the full request hash, so every new judge format misses it. I checked that old-2’s **1,620** judge calls have unique system and user text pairs. Use those pairs to find the stored calls, and compare the rest of each outgoing request with the old one except for the four permitted format changes. For the four refused first calls, explicitly feed the saved *accepted retry answer* to the matching first request and label the substitution. Prove rejection of the four originals separately through `model.call`. Compare the substantive saved judgements, including both push lists and `why_changed`, and verify the new request hashes and config separately. The existing comparison requires old hashes and leaves those answer fields out. A replay can also pass while the product is wrong if a harness validator enforces `maxItems` on its own: I confirmed that the real `model.check_schema` accepts `[\"v1\"]` under `maxItems: 0` today. Exercise all four citation fields, including empty lists, through that real validator. For T2, record the population explicitly: **5,415 archive rows**, **5,408 distinct request-answer pairs**, **5,389 committed**, **17 refused**, and **2 valid answers from the stopped control batch that were never committed**. [Existing replay](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/window_test.py:42) · [Store comparison](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/rebuild_control.py:37) · [Production array validator](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:217)\n\n6. **D712 covers the four lists and the checks needed to enforce them.** The size failure has a real precedent in D358. Describe how it uses the existing day-failure path and that retrying the same oversized request will hit the same limit. A second runnable judge version, a new retry policy, or a rule that drops evidence to fit would go beyond this slice. The next test should be the corrected $0 replay and its real-validator controls. [D711 and D712](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10679) · [Existing failure path](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/round.py:90)\n\nThis was a read-only review. I queried the saved archives and ran in-memory checks. No files changed and no model provider was called."}}
